---
const lanes = [
  {
    title: 'Event and wedding trailers',
    body: 'Luxury restroom trailers, VIP units, festival turns.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Construction and industrial',
    body: 'Jobsite units, office trailers, storage.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Relief and emergency',
    body: 'Shower units, first response, temporary housing.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section band" id="market">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <p class="kicker">The market the name sits on</p>
      <h2>The trailer industry keeps moving. This domain names it.</h2>
      <p>
        From wedding restroom trailers to units parked on construction sites, operators sell a simple promise: a clean, mobile room where the work or the event is. TinkleTrailers.com is the semantic home for that promise.
      </p>
      <p>It does not come with trucks or contracts. It comes with the words those businesses already use.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card stack">
      {lanes.map((lane) => (
        <div class="stack-row">
          <div>
            <h3>{lane.title}</h3>
            <p>{lane.body}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
